#doc(title: [Kinematics worksheet], subject: "Year 12 physics")

= Motion in a straight line

A car starts from rest and reaches a speed of #qty(18, "m s^-1") in #qty(6.0, "s") with a uniform acceleration.

Sketch a graph of the car's velocity against time for these #qty(6.0, "s"). Use the box below.

#figure(class: "working")[]

Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the car, using $v = u + a t$.

#figure(class: "answer")[]

Calculate the distance the car travels in this time, and explain how the graph you sketched shows this distance.

#figure(class: "answer long")[]

A ball is dropped from rest from a height of #qty(20, "m"). Take the acceleration of free fall as #qty(9.81, "m s^-2") and ignore air resistance.

Calculate the time the ball takes to reach the ground.

#figure(class: "answer")[]

Explain why an object falling freely near the surface of the Earth is said to move with uniform acceleration.

#figure(class: "answer")[]

= Answer space

The answers below are in the source, and the worksheet shows answer space in their place (SPEC §6.3).

A cyclist travels #qty(150, "m") in #qty(30, "s"). Calculate the cyclist's average speed.

#figure(class: "solution lined")[Average speed is distance over time: $v = 150 / 30 = 5.0$ m/s.]

Sketch the cyclist's distance against time.

#figure(class: "solution fixed")[A straight line through the origin with a gradient of 5.0 m/s.]

Show that a stone thrown upwards at #qty(12, "m s^-1") rises about #qty(7.3, "m").

#figure(class: "solution")[At the top $v = 0$, so $v^2 = u^2 - 2 g s$ gives
$ s = u^2 / (2 g) = 12^2 / (2 times 9.81) = 7.3 "m" $
The stone rises #qty(7.3, "m").]

#figure(class: "hint")[Hint: start from $v^2 = u^2 + 2 a s$, with $a = -g$.]

Explain why the stone takes as long to fall as to rise.

#figure(class: "solution")[The acceleration is the same on the way up and on the way down, so the motion is symmetric.]
